<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Phrae</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Phrae is a town and province on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yom-river">Yom River</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>. An old Tai principality, it was brought under the direct control of Chiang Mai by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tilokarat">Tilokarat</a> in the mid-15th century and later passed with the rest of Lan Na under Burmese and then Siamese suzerainty. It is known for its teak houses and traditional <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indigo">indigo</a>-dyed cloth.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/phrae.jpg" alt="Phrae" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anurak Sankhuean · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:3.%E0%B8%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9C%E0%B8%B9%E0%B9%89%E0%B8%A7%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%8A%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%88%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%94%E0%B9%81%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B9%88.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
